<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Supplementary Material</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters</h3>

<section id="A1.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.1 </span>MCCT</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">First, let’s revisit the calibration map defined in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 1. ‣ 3.1 MCCT ‣ 3 Method ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we have:</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z)=S(Z)\odot W+b" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z)=S(Z)\odot W+b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the purpose of calculating the gradient, we could ignore the constraints. To simplify the notation, instead of reverse sorting the transformed logits, here we remove the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> the inverse sorting operation, and instead of calculating the loss between the S(Z) and the permuted one-hot encoded label <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> that each vector <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math> is permuted in accordance to the sorting index of the corresponding logit vector <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{j}=\frac{e^{f(Z)_{j}}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}e^{f(Z)_{i}}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{j}=\frac{e^{f(Z)_{j}}}{\sum_{i=1}^{n}e^{f(Z)_{i}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The transformed logits are then go through softmax operation to produce the probability estimation <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="A1.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="L=-\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y_{j}\log\hat{p}_{j}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>Y</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=-\sum_{j=1}^{n}Y_{j}\log\hat{p}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">And the loss <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated by taking the Negative log-likelihood loss between the transform probability <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> and the sorted one-hot encoded logit <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)}=\hat{p}-Y" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)}=\hat{p}-Y</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Equation <a href="#A1.E4" title="In A.1.1 MCCT ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows the gradient vector of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z)</annotation></semantics></math>, this is the well known derivative of the Softmax Function combine with the Categorical Cross-Entropy Loss.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=S(Z)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=S(Z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Equation <a href="#A1.E5" title="In A.1.1 MCCT ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> describes the gradient of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial L}{\partial W}=\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)_{j}}\cdot\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=S(Z)\odot(\hat{p}-Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L}{\partial W}=\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)_{j}}\cdot\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=S(Z)\odot(\hat{p}-Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p">Then by using the chain rule we have the gradient vector of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> described in Equation <a href="#A1.E6" title="In A.1.1 MCCT ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a></p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial L}{\partial B}=\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)}\cdot\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial B}=(\hat{p}-Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L}{\partial B}=\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)}\cdot\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial B}=(\hat{p}-Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p">From equation <a href="#A1.E1" title="In A.1.1 MCCT ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> we know that the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial B}</annotation></semantics></math> is simply <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math>. Then by using the chain rule we have the gradient vector of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> described as in Equation <a href="#A1.E7" title="In A.1.1 MCCT ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">A.1.2 </span>MCCT-I</h4>

<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For the calibration map described in the Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2. ‣ 3.2 MCCT-I ‣ 3 Method ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> we have</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z)=\frac{S(Z)}{W}+b" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>W</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z)=\frac{S(Z)}{W}+b</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We can see that the <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial L}{\partial B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L}{\partial B}</annotation></semantics></math> is the same as the first calibration map.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=-\frac{S(Z)}{W^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=-\frac{S(Z)}{W^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Equation <a href="#A1.E9" title="In A.1.2 MCCT-I ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> describes the gradient of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(Z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(Z)</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial L}{\partial W}=\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)}\cdot\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=-\frac{S(Z)}{W^{2}}\odot(\hat{p}-Y)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>W</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>W</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial L}{\partial W}=\frac{\partial L}{\partial f(Z)}\cdot\frac{\partial f(Z)}{\partial W}=-\frac{S(Z)}{W^{2}}\odot(\hat{p}-Y),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Then by using the chain rule we have the gradient vector of <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A1.SS1.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>W</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W</annotation></semantics></math> described in Equation <a href="#A1.E10" title="In A.1.2 MCCT-I ‣ A.1 Gradient of MCCT and MCCT-I parameters ‣ Appendix A Supplementary Material ‣ Instance-Wise Monotonic Calibration by Constrained Transformation" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Additional information for Base Classifier</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For CIFAR-10 and CIFAR-100, we use the logits provided by previous work <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kull et al., 2019</a>]</cite>, available at <a href="https://github.com/markus93/NN_calibration" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/markus93/NN_calibration</a>. For ImageNet-1K, we use the PyTorch pre-trained models <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>]</cite> from <a href="https://pytorch.org/vision/main/models.html" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://pytorch.org/vision/main/models.html</a> and perform inference on the original ImageNet-1K test set, which is randomly divided 50-50 into a calibration set and a testing set.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</article>
</div>
